# Interactive shell: fish.
#
# One package, not three: autosuggestions and syntax highlighting are built into
# the fish reader, so the two zsh plugin formulae have no counterpart here.
#
# No plugin manager. fisher, oh-my-fish and Tide all install unreviewed code from
# GitHub at runtime, which is the trust boundary SECURITY.md draws around the
# Homebrew bootstrap. Everything this workstation asks of a shell — prompt,
# history, directory jumping, per-directory environments — is already provided by
# starship, atuin, zoxide and direnv, each of which supports fish directly.
brew "fish" # Interactive shell with native completion, highlighting and suggestions.
